# The credentials file (docs/security.md, section 2): a secret, one line per
# agent. Mount it read-only; the server re-reads it on change.
#
#   user   kanboard-user   kanboard-api-token   bearer-hashes   [emails]
#
# user: the agent's name here; what an OAuth token's user claim must carry.
# kanboard-user: the Kanboard user the agent acts as (its login name).
# kanboard-api-token: that user's personal API token (Kanboard: the user's
#   profile, "API"), or its password; the Basic password on /jsonrpc.php.
# bearer-hashes: comma-separated hex SHA-256 digests of the client secrets,
#   one per client, or -. Make one with:  printf '%s' "$SECRET" | node src/main.ts --hash
# emails: optional; comma-separated e-mail addresses, or -. Behind Cloudflare
#   Access (docs/cloudflare-access.md) the address Access signed in selects the
#   line. An address belongs to one line only.

writer-bot  writer-bot  kb_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx  3f1a…(64 hex digits)
reader-bot  reader      kb_yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy  9b2c…,4e7d…
web-bot     web-bot     kb_wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww  -                       web-bot@example.org
